invariant: INV-14
file: cpu_cfg.h
catches: test/host-builds.sh
reason: cpu_cfg.h's arm64 set gains CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA, so an arm64 object
  takes a bit that names x86-64 instructions and has no path for it, where
  the ruling is that an object refuses a bit of the other architecture and
  does not ignore it (docs/decisions.md 89). The rows of test/test_cpu.h
  catch it only on an arm64 machine, so the catch is the script: it reads
  the header for both architectures under the pinned clang and compares
  each set with the bits it writes out.

--- old
     CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA512 | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA3)
--- new
     CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA512 | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA3 |       \
     CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA)
